.TH SDL_iconv 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_iconv \- This function converts text between encodings, reading from and writing to a buffer.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "size_t SDL_iconv(SDL_iconv_t cd, const char **inbuf,
.BI "             size_t *inbytesleft, char **outbuf,
.BI "             size_t *outbytesleft);
.BI "
.BI "
.BI "#define SDL_ICONV_ERROR     (size_t)-1  /**< Generic error. Check SDL_GetError()? */
.BI "#define SDL_ICONV_E2BIG     (size_t)-2  /**< Output buffer was too small. */
.BI "#define SDL_ICONV_EILSEQ    (size_t)-3  /**< Invalid input sequence was encountered. */
.BI "#define SDL_ICONV_EINVAL    (size_t)-4  /**< Incomplete input sequence was encountered. */
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
It returns the number of successful conversions on success\[char46] On error,
.BR SDL_ICONV_E2BIG
is returned when the output buffer is too small, or
.BR SDL_ICONV_EILSEQ
is returned when an invalid input sequence is encountered, or
.BR SDL_ICONV_EINVAL
is returned when an incomplete input sequence is encountered\[char46]
.PP
On exit:
.PP

\(bu inbuf will point to the beginning of the next multibyte sequence\[char46] On error, this is the location of the problematic input sequence\[char46] On success, this is the end of the input sequence\[char46]
.PP
\(bu inbytesleft will be set to the number of bytes left to convert, which will be 0 on success\[char46]
.PP
\(bu outbuf will point to the location where to store the next output byte\[char46]
.PP
\(bu outbytesleft will be set to the number of bytes left in the output buffer\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I cd
The character set conversion context, created in
.BR SDL_iconv_open ()\[char46]

.TP
.I inbuf
Address of variable that points to the first character of the input sequence\[char46]
.TP
.I inbytesleft
The number of bytes in the input buffer\[char46]
.TP
.I outbuf
Address of variable that points to the output buffer\[char46]
.TP
.I outbytesleft
The number of bytes in the output buffer\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of conversions on success, or a negative error code\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
Do not use the same
.BR SDL_iconv_t
from two threads at once\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_iconv_open (3),
.BR SDL_iconv_close (3),
.BR SDL_iconv_string (3)
